 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration{{% available_from "v1.151.0" %}} allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway Instances API](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-servers-list-servers).
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway zone to discover instances in, e.g. "fr-par-1".
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#regions-and-zones for the list of available zones.
+  - zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # project_id is the id of the Scaleway project to discover instances in.
+    # Either project_id or organization_id must be set.
+    #
+    project_id: "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
+
+    # organization_id is the id of the Scaleway organization to discover instances in.
+    # It is used only if project_id isn't set.
+    #
+    # organization_id: "..."
+
+    # server is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # server: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # The secret key used for authenticating requests to the Scaleway API must be passed
+    # via the usual HTTP API client options below, e.g. via `headers: ["X-Auth-Token: <secret_key>"]`.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#authentication for details.
+    #
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<public_ipv4>:<port>`, where `<public_ipv4>` is the public IPv4 address of the instance, while `<port>` is the port specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs`.
+Instances without a public or a private IPv4 address are skipped, since there is nothing to scrape.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the instance, e.g. `DEV1-S`
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the state of the instance, e.g. `running` or `stopped`
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv6`: the public IPv6 address of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the id of the organization the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: the comma-separated list of tags of the instance
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
